+			return -EINVAL;
```
Reason:
This check immediately rejects any negative accessor index right after parsing the integer from the spec string. Since CO‑RE accessor indices (struct member indices, array indices, enumerator indices) are inherently non‑negative, this validation prevents the negative value from ever reaching the subsequent bounds checks or the member offset calculation, thereby eliminating the out‑of‑bounds read vulnerability.


